--- !u!114 &1813287775
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1813287773}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: fd6bda4aa472d574eb0de3283e1c33d6, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  _password: eagle11
  _noteText: "SECURITY LOG: #42-B STATION: ECHOES IN THE HULL OFFICER: K. JENSEN\n\nSTATUS:
    CRITICAL ERROR\n\nLOG CONTENT: The power grid in the Cafeteria is failing. Someone
    \u2014 or something \u2014 is chewing through the cables in the vents. It\u2019s
    not just the hull cooling down anymore. We can hear them...\n\nThey aren't just
    scratching. They are mimicking. Yesterday I heard the sound of a hydraulic door
    opening in Sector B, but when I checked the monitors, the sector was empty. It\u2019s
    trying to lure us out.\n\nIf you are reading this, do NOT follow the sounds.
    Do not trust the station's automated signals.\n\nI don't know what happened to
    Officer Tyler. He was in the Security Module when the screaming started. Tyler,
    if you can hear this through the internal comms \u2014 stay locked in. Do not
    open the blast doors for anyone. Not even for me.\n\nWe brought IT on board to
    study IT. That was our biggest mistake. It\u2019s awake now. Everyone in the
    Command Module is gone.\n\nIf you can reach the escape pods, you need to manually
    override the\u2014 [SYSTEM ERROR] [SIGNAL LOST]\n\nhsdghasdbglhw4590t834t...
    IT IS BEHIND THE SCREEN DO NOT LOOK UP asdgashdg..."
  _minYClamp: -0.2
  _maxYClamp: 0.179
  _scrollSpeed: -0.05
